{"id":"4cdb2db63d52cfb5f6c9199e2d08196f2bb9dc77","axis":"silent","repo":"aquasecurity/trivy","sha":"4cdb2db63d52cfb5f6c9199e2d08196f2bb9dc77","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/guide/configuration/others.md","lines":["@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ $ trivy image --scanners vuln alpine:3.15"," | Misconfiguration |     ✓     |"," |      Secret      |     ✓     |"," |     License      |     ✓     |","+|      Crypto      |     ✓     |"," "," By default, `Trivy` exits with code 0 even when security issues are detected."," Use the `--exit-code` option if you want to exit with a non-zero exit code."],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/guide/configuration/reporting.md","lines":["@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ Trivy supports the following formats:"," | Misconfiguration |     ✓     |"," |      Secret      |     ✓     |"," |     License      |     ✓     |","+|      Crypto      |     ✓     |"," "," ```bash"," $ trivy image -f table golang:1.22.11-alpine3.20"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/guide/references/configuration/cli/trivy_convert.md","lines":["@@ -41,7 +41,13 @@ trivy convert [flags] RESULT_JSON","   -o, --output string              output file name","       --output-plugin-arg string   [EXPERIMENTAL] output plugin arguments","       --report string              specify a report format for the output (allowed values: all,summary) (default \"all\")","-      --scanners strings           List of scanners included when generating the json report. Used only for rendering the summary table. (allowed values: vuln,misconfig,secret,license)","+      --scanners strings           List of scanners included when generating the json report. Used only for rendering the summary table.","+                                   Allowed values:","+                                     - vuln","+                                     - misconfig","+                                     - secret","+                                     - license","+                                     - crypto","   -s, --severity strings           severities of security issues to be displayed","                                    Allowed values:","                                      - UNKNOWN"],"additions":7,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/guide/scanner/crypto.md","lines":["@@ -3,13 +3,12 @@"," !!! warning \"EXPERIMENTAL\"","     This feature might change without preserving backwards compatibility."," ","-Trivy inventories the cryptographic material it finds in a container image and reports it as a CBOM (Cryptography Bill of Materials). The CBOM lists the certificates and keys themselves and the algorithms they use. The result is part of the CycloneDX report, next to the software components. In JSON output Trivy also reports [weak assets](#findings) found by built-in checks.","+Trivy inventories the cryptographic material it finds in a container image and reports it as a CBOM (Cryptography Bill of Materials). The CBOM lists the certificates and keys themselves and the algorithms they use. The result is part of the CycloneDX report, next to the software components. In JSON and table output Trivy also reports [weak assets](#findings) found by built-in checks."," ","-The scanner is off by default. Enable it with `--scanners crypto` together with `--format cyclonedx` or `--format json`.","+The scanner is off by default. Enable it with `--scanners crypto` together with `--format cyclonedx`, `--format json` or `--format table`."," "," ```shell"," $ trivy image --scanners crypto --format cyclonedx --output result.cdx.json myimage:1.0.0","-$ trivy image --scanners crypto --format json --output result.json myimage:1.0.0"," ```"," "," Trivy rejects `--scanners crypto` with other report formats.","@@ -114,7 +113,7 @@ The parameters of an algorithm are stored in `algorithmProperties`. The key size"," "," ## Findings"," ","-Trivy runs built-in checks to find weak cryptographic assets and reports the findings in JSON output. Trivy does not determine whether any software uses these assets.","+Trivy runs built-in checks to find weak cryptographic assets and reports the findings in JSON and table output. Trivy does not determine whether any software uses these assets."," "," | Rule ID | Title | Asset | Condition | Severity |"," | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |","@@ -167,7 +166,28 @@ Every entry of `CryptoAssets` in JSON output has an `AssetID`, and a finding ref"," | `CRYPTO-0003` | `Curve`, `ClassicalSecurityLevel` |"," | `CRYPTO-0004` | `NotAfter` |"," ","-Findings are evaluated only for JSON output, so they do not affect the exit code of CycloneDX output. `trivy convert` keeps the findings of a JSON report only when converting to JSON, and keeps the cryptographic assets for any format.","+Table output shows the findings without the inventory. Identical rows are merged and the asset name ends with their number, such as `x2`. `Total` counts every finding, and JSON output tells the assets apart.","+","+```","+example:latest (crypto)","+=======================","+Total: 4 (UNKNOWN: 0, LOW: 0, MEDIUM: 1, HIGH: 3, CRITICAL: 0)","+","+┌──────────┬─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────┐","+│ Severity │   Rule ID   │               Asset               │         File         │                   Message                   │","+├──────────┼─────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤","+│ HIGH     │ CRYPTO-0002 │ RSA-1024 private key (PKCS#8)     │ app/certs/legacy.key │ RSA key is 1024 bits, less than 2048        │","+│          │             │                                   │                      │ https://avd.aquasec.com/crypto/crypto-0002/ │","+│          │             ├───────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────┤                                             │","+│          │             │ RSA-1024 public key (PKIX) x2     │ app/certs/legacy.pem │                                             │","+│          │             │                                   │                      │                                             │","+├──────────┼─────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┤                      ├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤","+│ MEDIUM   │ CRYPTO-0004 │ CN=legacy.example.com certificate │                      │ Certificate expired on 2024-03-01           │","+│          │             │                                   │                      │ https://avd.aquasec.com/crypto/crypto-0004/ │","+└──────────┴─────────────┴───────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────┘","+```","+","+Findings are evaluated only for JSON and table output, so they do not affect the exit code of CycloneDX output. `trivy convert` keeps the findings of a JSON report only when converting to JSON or table, and keeps the cryptographic assets for any format."," "," A rule ID in an [ignore file](../configuration/filtering.md#by-finding-ids) suppresses its findings, and the `crypto` section of `.trivyignore.yaml` can limit that to some file paths. The assets of suppressed findings stay in the inventory. `--ignore-policy` and `--show-suppressed` do not apply to crypto findings."," "],"additions":25,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/guide/target/container_image.md","lines":["@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@ $ trivy image --scanners license [YOUR_IMAGE_NAME]"," "," ### Cryptographic assets"," It is experimental and disabled by default.","-It requires the CycloneDX or JSON format.","+It requires the CycloneDX, JSON or table format."," See [here](../scanner/crypto.md) for the detail."," "," ```shell"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/commands/app.go","lines":["@@ -546,6 +546,7 @@ func NewConvertCommand(globalFlags *flag.GlobalFlagGroup) *cobra.Command {"," \t\tScanners: flag.ScannersFlag.Clone(),"," \t}"," \tscanFlagGroup.Scanners.Default = nil // disable default scanners","+\tscanFlagGroup.Scanners.Values = append(scanFlagGroup.Scanners.Values, string(types.CryptoScanner))"," \tscanFlagGroup.Scanners.Usage = \"List of scanners included when generating the json report. Used only for rendering the summary table.\""," "," \tconvertFlags := flag.Flags{"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/commands/convert/run.go","lines":["@@ -41,10 +41,11 @@ func Run(ctx context.Context, opts flag.Options) (err error) {"," \t}"," "," \tcompat(&r)","-\t// Only JSON output shows crypto findings","-\tif opts.Format != types.FormatJSON {","+","+\tif !slices.Contains(types.CryptoFindingsFormats, opts.Format) {"," \t\tr.Results.DropCryptoFindings()"," \t}","+"," \tif err = result.Filter(ctx, r, opts.FilterOpts()); err != nil {"," \t\treturn xerrors.Errorf(\"unable to filter results: %w\", err)"," \t}"],"additions":3,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/crypto/check/check.go","lines":["@@ -20,6 +20,19 @@ type rule struct {"," \t// match reports whether the asset fails the rule and returns the evidence."," \t// Unknown asset values never match."," \tmatch func(asset ftypes.CryptoAsset, now time.Time) (types.CryptoEvidence, bool)","+\t// message describes the failed check by its evidence.","+\tmessage func(evidence types.CryptoEvidence) string","+}","+","+// Message returns the text that describes why the finding was reported.","+// It is empty for a finding of an unknown rule or a rule without a description.","+func Message(finding types.CryptoFinding) string {","+\tfor _, r := range rules {","+\t\tif r.id == finding.RuleID && r.message != nil {","+\t\t\treturn r.message(finding.Evidence)","+\t\t}","+\t}","+\treturn \"\""," }"," "," // match is a finding together with the asset it refers to."],"additions":13,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/crypto/check/check_test.go","lines":["@@ -274,3 +274,62 @@ func TestEvaluate(t *testing.T) {"," \t\t})"," \t}"," }","+","+func TestMessage(t *testing.T) {","+\ttests := []struct {","+\t\tname    string","+\t\tfinding types.CryptoFinding","+\t\twant    string","+\t}{","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname: \"SHA-1 signature\",","+\t\t\tfinding: types.CryptoFinding{","+\t\t\t\tRuleID:   \"CRYPTO-0001\",","+\t\t\t\tEvidence: types.CryptoEvidence{SignatureAlgorithm: \"RSA-PKCS1-1.5-SHA-1\"},","+\t\t\t},","+\t\t\twant: \"Certificate is signed with RSA-PKCS1-1.5-SHA-1\",","+\t\t},","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname: \"small RSA key\",","+\t\t\tfinding: types.CryptoFinding{","+\t\t\t\tRuleID:   \"CRYPTO-0002\",","+\t\t\t\tEvidence: types.CryptoEvidence{KeySize: 1024},","+\t\t\t},","+\t\t\twant: \"RSA key is 1024 bits, less than 2048\",","+\t\t},","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname: \"weak curve\",","+\t\t\tfinding: types.CryptoFinding{","+\t\t\t\tRuleID:   \"CRYPTO-0003\",","+\t\t\t\tEvidence: types.CryptoEvidence{Curve: \"P-192\", ClassicalSecurityLevel: new(96)},","+\t\t\t},","+\t\t\twant: \"Curve P-192 gives 96 bits of security, less than 112\",","+\t\t},","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname: \"weak curve without a name\",","+\t\t\tfinding: types.CryptoFinding{","+\t\t\t\tRuleID:   \"CRYPTO-0003\",","+\t\t\t\tEvidence: types.CryptoEvidence{ClassicalSecurityLevel: new(96)},","+\t\t\t},","+\t\t\twant: \"Elliptic curve gives 96 bits of security, less than 112\",","+\t\t},","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname: \"expired certificate\",","+\t\t\tfinding: types.CryptoFinding{","+\t\t\t\tRuleID:   \"CRYPTO-0004\",","+\t\t\t\tEvidence: types.CryptoEvidence{NotAfter: time.Date(2024, 3, 1, 12, 0, 0, 0, time.UTC)},","+\t\t\t},","+\t\t\twant: \"Certificate expired on 2024-03-01\",","+\t\t},","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname:    \"unknown rule\",","+\t\t\tfinding: types.CryptoFinding{RuleID: \"CRYPTO-9999\"},","+\t\t},","+\t}","+","+\tfor _, tt := range tests {","+\t\tt.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {","+\t\t\tassert.Equal(t, tt.want, check.Message(tt.finding))","+\t\t})","+\t}","+}"],"additions":59,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/crypto/check/rules.go","lines":["@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@"," package check"," "," import (","+\t\"fmt\""," \t\"slices\""," \t\"time\""," ","@@ -17,6 +18,7 @@ var rules = []rule{"," \t\tseverity: dbTypes.SeverityMedium,"," \t\tkind:     ftypes.CryptoKindCertificate,"," \t\tmatch:    matchSHA1Signature,","+\t\tmessage:  sha1SignatureMessage,"," \t},"," \t{"," \t\tid:       \"CRYPTO-0002\",","@@ -24,6 +26,7 @@ var rules = []rule{"," \t\tseverity: dbTypes.SeverityHigh,"," \t\tkind:     ftypes.CryptoKindKey,"," \t\tmatch:    matchSmallRSAKey,","+\t\tmessage:  smallRSAKeyMessage,"," \t},"," \t{"," \t\tid:       \"CRYPTO-0003\",","@@ -31,6 +34,7 @@ var rules = []rule{"," \t\tseverity: dbTypes.SeverityHigh,"," \t\tkind:     ftypes.CryptoKindAlgorithm,"," \t\tmatch:    matchWeakCurve,","+\t\tmessage:  weakCurveMessage,"," \t},"," \t{"," \t\tid:       \"CRYPTO-0004\",","@@ -38,6 +42,7 @@ var rules = []rule{"," \t\tseverity: dbTypes.SeverityMedium,"," \t\tkind:     ftypes.CryptoKindCertificate,"," \t\tmatch:    matchExpiredCertificate,","+\t\tmessage:  expiredCertificateMessage,"," \t},"," }"," ","@@ -48,6 +53,13 @@ const ("," \toidECPublicKey = \"1.2.840.10045.2.1\""," )"," ","+const (","+\t// minRSAKeySize is the smallest RSA key size in bits that passes CRYPTO-0002.","+\tminRSAKeySize = 2048","+\t// minSecurityLevel is the smallest classical security level in bits that passes CRYPTO-0003.","+\tminSecurityLevel = 112","+)","+"," // sha1SignatureOIDs are the signature algorithms that hash with SHA-1. RSASSA-PSS names its"," // hash in parameters that are not collected, so it is left out."," var sha1SignatureOIDs = []string{","@@ -69,7 +81,7 @@ func matchSHA1Signature(asset ftypes.CryptoAsset, _ time.Time) (types.CryptoEvid"," }"," "," func matchSmallRSAKey(asset ftypes.CryptoAsset, _ time.Time) (types.CryptoEvidence, bool) {","-\tif asset.Key == nil || asset.Key.Size <= 0 || asset.Key.Size >= 2048 {","+\tif asset.Key == nil || asset.Key.Size <= 0 || asset.Key.Size >= minRSAKeySize {"," \t\treturn types.CryptoEvidence{}, false"," \t}"," \talgorithm, found := relatedAlgorithm(asset, ftypes.CryptoRelationshipUsedWith)","@@ -87,7 +99,7 @@ func matchWeakCurve(asset ftypes.CryptoAsset, _ time.Time) (types.CryptoEvidence"," \t\treturn types.CryptoEvidence{}, false"," \t}"," \tlevel := asset.Algorithm.ClassicalSecurityLevel","-\tif level == nil || *level >= 112 {","+\tif level == nil || *level >= minSecurityLevel {"," \t\treturn types.CryptoEvidence{}, false"," \t}"," \t// The curve is only evidence, so a parse error is ignored.","@@ -108,6 +120,30 @@ func matchExpiredCertificate(asset ftypes.CryptoAsset, now time.Time) (types.Cry"," \t}, true"," }"," ","+func sha1SignatureMessage(e types.CryptoEvidence) string {","+\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"Certificate is signed with %s\", e.SignatureAlgorithm)","+}","+","+func smallRSAKeyMessage(e types.CryptoEvidence) string {","+\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"RSA key is %d bits, less than %d\", e.KeySize, minRSAKeySize)","+}","+","+func weakCurveMessage(e types.CryptoEvidence) string {","+\tcurve := \"Elliptic curve\"","+\tif e.Curve != \"\" {","+\t\tcurve = \"Curve \" + e.Curve","+\t}","+\tlevel := 0","+\tif e.ClassicalSecurityLevel != nil {","+\t\tlevel = *e.ClassicalSecurityLevel","+\t}","+\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s gives %d bits of security, less than %d\", curve, level, minSecurityLevel)","+}","+","+func expiredCertificateMessage(e types.CryptoEvidence) string {","+\treturn \"Certificate expired on \" + e.NotAfter.UTC().Format(\"2006-01-02\")","+}","+"," // relatedAlgorithm returns the identity of the algorithm the asset has the given"," // relationship with."," func relatedAlgorithm(asset ftypes.CryptoAsset, relationship ftypes.CryptoRelationshipType) (ftypes.CryptoIdentity, bool) {"],"additions":38,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/flag/options.go","lines":["@@ -449,6 +449,9 @@ type Options struct {"," \tusedFlags []Flagger"," }"," ","+// cryptoFormats are the formats that show cryptographic assets or their findings.","+var cryptoFormats = slices.Concat([]types.Format{types.FormatCycloneDX}, types.CryptoFindingsFormats)","+"," // Align takes consistency of options"," func (o *Options) Align(f *Flags) error {"," \tif scanFlagGroup, ok := findFlagGroup[*ScanFlagGroup](f); ok && scanFlagGroup.Scanners != nil {","@@ -488,9 +491,8 @@ func (o *Options) Align(f *Flags) error {"," \t\t}"," \t}"," ","-\t// Only JSON and CycloneDX output show cryptographic assets","-\tif o.Scanners.Enabled(types.CryptoScanner) && o.Format != types.FormatCycloneDX && o.Format != types.FormatJSON {","-\t\treturn xerrors.Errorf(\"'--scanners crypto' can only be used with '--format cyclonedx' or '--format json'\")","+\tif o.Scanners.Enabled(types.CryptoScanner) && !slices.Contains(cryptoFormats, o.Format) {","+\t\treturn xerrors.Errorf(\"'--scanners crypto' can only be used with '--format cyclonedx', '--format json' or '--format table'\")"," \t}"," "," \t// A remote SBOM replaces layer analysis, so cryptographic assets would not be collected","@@ -532,8 +534,7 @@ func (o *Options) ScanOpts() types.ScanOptions {"," \t\tScanRemovedPackages: o.ScanRemovedPkgs,     // this is valid only for 'image' subcommand"," \t\tLicenseCategories:   o.LicenseCategories,"," \t\tLicenseFull:         o.LicenseFull,","-\t\t// Only JSON output shows crypto findings","-\t\tCryptoChecks:        o.Format == types.FormatJSON,","+\t\tCryptoChecks:        slices.Contains(types.CryptoFindingsFormats, o.Format),"," \t\tFilePatterns:        o.FilePatterns,"," \t\tIncludeDevDeps:      o.IncludeDevDeps,"," \t\tDistro:              o.Distro,"],"additions":6,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/flag/options_test.go","lines":["@@ -382,7 +382,14 @@ func TestOptions_Align(t *testing.T) {"," \t\t\t\tReportOptions: flag.ReportOptions{Format: types.FormatTable},"," \t\t\t\tScanOptions:   flag.ScanOptions{Scanners: types.Scanners{types.CryptoScanner}},"," \t\t\t},","-\t\t\twantErr: \"'--scanners crypto' can only be used with '--format cyclonedx' or '--format json'\",","+\t\t},","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname: \"crypto scanner with SARIF\",","+\t\t\topts: flag.Options{","+\t\t\t\tReportOptions: flag.ReportOptions{Format: types.FormatSarif},","+\t\t\t\tScanOptions:   flag.ScanOptions{Scanners: types.Scanners{types.CryptoScanner}},","+\t\t\t},","+\t\t\twantErr: \"'--scanners crypto' can only be used with '--format cyclonedx', '--format json' or '--format table'\","," \t\t},"," \t\t{"," \t\t\tname: \"crypto scanner with SBOM sources\",","@@ -425,3 +432,36 @@ func TestOptions_Align(t *testing.T) {"," \t\t})"," \t}"," }","+","+func TestOptions_ScanOpts_cryptoChecks(t *testing.T) {","+\ttests := []struct {","+\t\tname   string","+\t\tformat types.Format","+\t\twant   bool","+\t}{","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname:   \"JSON\",","+\t\t\tformat: types.FormatJSON,","+\t\t\twant:   true,","+\t\t},","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname:   \"table\",","+\t\t\tformat: types.FormatTable,","+\t\t\twant:   true,","+\t\t},","+\t\t{","+\t\t\tname:   \"CycloneDX\",","+\t\t\tformat: types.FormatCycloneDX,","+\t\t\twant:   false,","+\t\t},","+\t}","+","+\tfor _, tt := range tests {","+\t\tt.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {","+\t\t\topts := flag.Options{","+\t\t\t\tReportOptions: flag.ReportOptions{Format: tt.format},","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t\tassert.Equal(t, tt.want, opts.ScanOpts().CryptoChecks)","+\t\t})","+\t}","+}"],"additions":41,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/report/table/crypto.go","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,128 @@","+package table","+","+import (","+\t\"bytes\"","+\t\"cmp\"","+\t\"fmt\"","+\t\"slices\"","+\t\"strings\"","+","+\t\"github.com/samber/lo\"","+","+\t\"github.com/aquasecurity/tml\"","+\tdbTypes \"github.com/aquasecurity/trivy-db/pkg/types\"","+\t\"github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/pkg/crypto/check\"","+\tftypes \"github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/pkg/fanal/types\"","+\t\"github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/pkg/types\"","+)","+","+type cryptoRenderer struct {","+\tw          *bytes.Buffer","+\tisTerminal bool","+\tseverities []dbTypes.Severity","+}","+","+func NewCryptoRenderer(buf *bytes.Buffer, isTerminal bool, severities []dbTypes.Severity) *cryptoRenderer {","+\tif !isTerminal {","+\t\ttml.DisableFormatting()","+\t}","+\treturn &cryptoRenderer{","+\t\tw:          buf,","+\t\tisTerminal: isTerminal,","+\t\tseverities: severities,","+\t}","+}","+","+func (r *cryptoRenderer) Render(result types.Result) {","+\tif len(result.CryptoFindings) == 0 {","+\t\treturn","+\t}","+","+\tassets := make(map[string]ftypes.CryptoAsset, len(result.CryptoAssets))","+\tfor _, asset := range result.CryptoAssets {","+\t\tassets[asset.AssetID] = asset","+\t}","+","+\tfindings := slices.Clone(result.CryptoFindings)","+\tslices.SortStableFunc(findings, func(a, b types.CryptoFinding) int {","+\t\tassetA, assetB := assets[a.AssetID], assets[b.AssetID]","+\t\treturn cmp.Or(","+\t\t\tdbTypes.CompareSeverityString(a.Severity, b.Severity),","+\t\t\tcmp.Compare(a.RuleID, b.RuleID),","+\t\t\tcmp.Compare(assetA.FilePath, assetB.FilePath),","+\t\t\tcmp.Compare(cryptoAssetLabel(assetA), cryptoAssetLabel(assetB)),","+\t\t\tcmp.Compare(check.Message(a), check.Message(b)),","+\t\t)","+\t})","+","+\tseverityCount := lo.CountValuesBy(findings, func(f types.CryptoFinding) string {","+\t\treturn f.Severity","+\t})","+\ttotal, summaries := summarize(r.severities, severityCount)","+","+\tRenderTarget(r.w, result.Target+\" (crypto)\", r.isTerminal)","+\tfmt.Fprintf(r.w, \"Total: %d (%s)\\n\\n\", total, strings.Join(summaries, \", \"))","+","+\ttw := newTableWriter(r.w, r.isTerminal)","+\ttw.SetHeaders(\"Severity\", \"Rule ID\", \"Asset\", \"File\", \"Message\")","+\tfor _, row := range groupCryptoFindings(findings, assets) {","+\t\tf := row.finding","+\t\tseverity := f.Severity","+\t\tif r.isTerminal {","+\t\t\tseverity = ColorizeSeverity(f.Severity, f.Severity)","+\t\t}","+\t\tlabel := cryptoAssetLabel(row.asset)","+\t\tif row.count > 1 {","+\t\t\tlabel = fmt.Sprintf(\"%s x%d\", label, row.count)","+\t\t}","+\t\tmessage := tml.Sprintf(\"%s\\n<blue>%s</blue>\", check.Message(f), cryptoRuleURL(f.RuleID))","+\t\ttw.AddRow(severity, f.RuleID, label, row.asset.FilePath, message)","+\t}","+\ttw.Render()","+}","+","+// cryptoRow is a table row for findings that look the same.","+type cryptoRow struct {","+\tfinding types.CryptoFinding","+\tasset   ftypes.CryptoAsset","+\tcount   int","+}","+","+// groupCryptoFindings joins neighboring findings of different assets that show the same values in the table.","+// The findings must be sorted.","+func groupCryptoFindings(findings []types.CryptoFinding, assets map[string]ftypes.CryptoAsset) []cryptoRow {","+\tvar rows []cryptoRow","+\tfor _, f := range findings {","+\t\tasset := assets[f.AssetID]","+\t\tif n := len(rows); n > 0 {","+\t\t\tprev := rows[n-1]","+\t\t\tif prev.finding.Severity == f.Severity && prev.finding.RuleID == f.RuleID &&","+\t\t\t\tprev.asset.FilePath == asset.FilePath && cryptoAssetLabel(prev.asset) == cryptoAssetLabel(asset) &&","+\t\t\t\tcheck.Message(prev.finding) == check.Message(f) {","+\t\t\t\trows[n-1].count++","+\t\t\t\tcontinue","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t}","+\t\trows = append(rows, cryptoRow{finding: f, asset: asset, count: 1})","+\t}","+\treturn rows","+}","+","+func cryptoRuleURL(ruleID string) string {","+\treturn \"https://avd.aquasec.com/crypto/\" + strings.ToLower(ruleID) + \"/\"","+}","+","+func cryptoAssetLabel(a ftypes.CryptoAsset) string {","+\tname := a.Name","+\tswitch a.Kind {","+\tcase ftypes.CryptoKindCertificate:","+\t\tname += \" certificate\"","+\tcase ftypes.CryptoKindAlgorithm:","+\t\tname += \" algorithm\"","+\t}","+\tif a.Format == \"\" {","+\t\treturn name","+\t}","+\t// The format keeps the same key in different containers from being merged into one cell.","+\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s (%s)\", name, a.Format)","+}"],"additions":128,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/report/table/crypto_test.go","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,283 @@","+package table_test","+","+import (","+\t\"bytes\"","+\t\"testing\"","+\t\"time\"","+","+\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/assert\"","+","+\tdbTy